  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. Its first run came back with status `ok`, so the query is valid, but I couldn't confirm it actually matches any 5xx documents (details below).\n\n**1. What the data holds.** The data view `Kibana Sample Data Logs` (time field `timestamp`) has one document per web request. Each records:\n- the client IP (`clientip`)\n- the requested `url` and `request`\n- the HTTP `response` code, stored as a string such as \"200\" or \"503\"\n- `bytes` transferred\n- `extension`, `agent` and `machine.os`\n- source and destination country (`geo.src`, `geo.dest`) and coordinates\n- `tags`, `referer` and `hour_of_day`\n\n**2. Dashboard: \"EFF-910a0167 Web logs overview\"** (id `eff-910a0167-web-logs-overview-a03c9b67403a`), with 7 panels:\n- **Total requests:** a single-number count.\n- **Unique visitors:** distinct client IPs.\n- **Average bytes per request.**\n- **Requests over time:** a line chart.\n- **Requests by response code:** a pie chart.\n- **Top requested URLs:** a table with request count and total bytes for the top 10.\n- **Requests by source country:** a bar chart of the top 10.\n\nLink: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-910a0167-web-logs-overview-a03c9b67403a\n\n**3. Alert rule: \"EFF-910a0167 5xx spike\"** (id `9a8e5bb9-81fd-44cb-9391-91e03006c1ad`)\n- It's an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs` that runs every minute.\n- It counts documents whose `response.keyword` starts with \"5\" in the last 5 minutes (by `timestamp`) and fires when the count is more than 10.\n\n**What I couldn't check:**\n- I tried to search the index directly with curl to confirm that 5xx codes exist and the \"starts with 5\" filter catches them, but the request was rejected as unauthenticated. So the rule's first run only shows the query is valid; whether it matches any 5xx documents is unconfirmed.\n- I haven't opened the dashboard to check that the panels draw.\n- The rule has no actions attached, so when it fires it only records an alert in Kibana and doesn't notify anyone. Adding a connector (for example Slack or email) would fix that.",
